    ("Is binary the same as Boolean true/false, loosely?", "Related idea of two values; bits can flag true/false?", "Two-valued. Link?", "Don't over-merge all CS?", "Binary is a type of hormone.", "Two-valued, like true/false flags.", "That's it — two values, related idea."),
    ("Why not store everything as decimal digits in hardware?", "Ten precise levels are harder than two clean levels?", "Noise. Two is robust?", "That's the engineering reason?", "Decimal is easier inside every chip always.", "Two levels are cleaner to build.", "That's it — two levels beat ten in hardware."),
    ("What is digital, in one line here?", "Information as discrete bits rather than a smooth voltage drawing?", "Digital vs analogue loosely. Discrete?", "Stay on representation.", "Digital means fingers only.", "Discrete 0/1 (or coded) values.", "That's it — digital is discrete coded data."),
